# Synthetic EDAC trace — CE storm followed by UE on the same DIMM rank.
#
# This is a synthetic, anonymized example trace illustrating the pattern of a
# correctable-error storm that precedes an uncorrectable error on the same csrow.
# No real production incident, system, or host is represented.
#
# Pattern:
#   - CEs begin on csrow 0, channel 0 at t=0
#   - CE rate accelerates (~doubling every 10 seconds)
#   - At t=47s, a UE occurs on the same csrow — the DIMM has failed
#   - The kernel calls memory_failure() on the affected page
#
# To replay:
#   python3 ../parse_edac_trace.py --input sample_ce_storm.log --output /tmp/ce_storm.json --pretty
#   sudo bash ../replay_kernel_state.sh --events /tmp/ce_storm.json
#
# To replay without UE injection (safer):
#   sudo bash ../replay_kernel_state.sh --events /tmp/ce_storm.json --skip-types UE

